course: dictionary
lesson: 5194
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Context means the words and sentences around a word. Jade is a good example, because it can mean a stone, a colour, or a name.
explain: «Jade in Wales put a fake sign on her brother's chair» Here Jade is a girl's name, because she is the one doing the joke. Ask yourself what fits: a stone cannot play a joke, but a person can.
explain: «Families look at the full moon for the lady Cháng'é and her jade rabbit.» Now ask again: is it a name, a colour, or a stone? The rabbit is a thing in a story, so jade here is a material or a colour, not a person. Try swapping in your meaning to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Jade is a hard green stone, used to make jewellery and carvings.
fact: Jade is also a green colour, so a jade scarf is a green scarf.
fact: «Jaded» means tired and bored, and long ago a jade was a worn-out horse.
fact: Jade is also a girl's name, so a capital J in a sentence can mean a person.
exercise: «Jade in Wales put a fake sign on her brother's chair.» In this sentence, what is Jade? | A green colour | A hard green stone | *A girl's name | A worn-out horse
exercise: Her jade scarf matched the leaves in spring. What does jade mean here? | A tired old horse | A girl's name | *A green colour | A hard green stone for carving
exercise: He felt jaded after a week of the same boring jobs. What does jaded mean? | Shiny, like a carved stone | *Tired and bored | Full of energy and ready to run | Very green, like a leaf
test: The carver turned the jade into a small rabbit. What is jade in this sentence? | A girl's name | *A hard green stone | A tired horse | A colour only, like paint
test: Jade asked if she could have a turn on the bike. What is Jade in this sentence? | A worn-out horse | *A girl's name | A hard stone for jewellery | A green colour
exam: The jaded old horse trotted slowly home after the long day. What does jaded mean here? | A girl's name | Hard and cold like a stone | *Tired and worn-out | Shiny and green
